# The coefficients of the product of two polynomials of 2-limb coefficients (milestone2.md, "sum,
# dot, axpy, convolution": conv_k; "The product of polynomials"): x of n_x coefficients and y of
# n_y, z of n_x + n_y - 1 (none when a polynomial is empty). Coefficient j is the dot product dot_2,
# in its sequential order, of the terms (x_i, y_(j-i)), i from max(0, j - n_y + 1) to
# min(j, n_x - 1) in increasing order: if every coefficient is canonical, each coefficient that is
# finite satisfies the statement of dot_2 for its own m_j terms, m_j <= min(n_x, n_y), so that the
# exported bound of dot for min(n_x, n_y) terms covers every one. The program supplies x and y,
# which the step only multiplies (rule R3). A convolution (architecture.md, "Convolutions"): the
# mask finite is the and of the tests of the coefficients, and when it is false a second pass makes
# every coefficient that is not finite the canonical NaN ("When something is not finite"). The array
# written overlaps neither x nor y.
fold:          conv_2
arrays:        supplied x = x0 x1, supplied y = y0 y1
coefficients:  dot_2
state:         mask finite
combine:       finite = and(finite, finite)
orders:        sequential
writes:        z = z0 z1
check:         fold_finish_2
finish:        none
value:         x*y
requires:      canonical x
requires:      canonical y
ensures:       coefficients z
ensures:       finite_or_nan z flag=finite
min_precision: 4
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
source:        dot_2 on the terms of each coefficient
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
